The last step to compute the features is applying a stati-
stical analysis of the combined distance over a temporal sli-
ding window of size W packets. The width W of the rolling
window has an important role on the classiﬁcation accuracy
of the crowd-counting system. In fact, increasing the win-
dow size allows to collect and process more data, improving
the performance, but at the same time also increasing the
estimation delay. The statistical moments have been evalua-
ted using both the distance between consecutive CSIs and
between all pairs of CSIs within the sliding window. Consi-
dering all the distances within a temporal window can lead
to extract features that are more informative for the crowd
density recognition. The statistical analysis was performed
through the ﬁrst and second order statistical moments, so
the extracted features are the following:
