6. CONCLUSION
In conclusion, to the best of our knowledge, this is the
ﬁrst WiFi-based device-free crowd counting method which
does not require to train the system exactly in the same
room/environment where the system is also tested. First
of all, the presented confusion matrices prove the eﬀecti-
veness of our approach for the crowd counting and crowd
density estimation. In fact, concerning crowd counting, esti-
mation errors are less or equal to 2 persons 91% and 81%
of time, while concerning crowd density estimation, avera-
ge accuracies are 74% and 52% in the rooms where a spe-
ciﬁc training is not carried out.Some future directions of
this work includes: study of the occupancy dynamics; esti-
mation of larger crowd in larger rooms; evaluate the im-
pact of the transmitter and receiver locations on the system
performance.
